select 'PRJ-00016', 'Identity and Access Platform', 'Replacement of three separate authentication mechanisms with a single identity platform covering colleagues, members and advisers, including multi-factor authentication throughout.', 'Critical', 'Active', 'Hypercare', 'Closure', 'Green', 'High', '2025-07-07', '2026-09-25', '2025-07-07', '2026-09-25', '2026-07-31', 96, 'All three populations are migrated and multi-factor authentication is enforced. Hypercare has been quiet: nine tickets in four weeks, all resolved, none critical. Closure documentation is being assembled.', 'Complete the closure report and lessons learned, hand over to application support on 25 September, and close the project at the September governance meeting.', 'Single identity platform for colleague, member and adviser authentication; multi-factor authentication for all three; single sign-on across internal applications; self-service password reset; and decommissioning of the three legacy authentication mechanisms.', 'Privileged access management and device management, both handled by separate security workstreams.', null, null, 'Green', 'Green', 'Green', 'Green', 'Green', false,
    (select id from public.programmes where programme_code = 'PRG-00005'),
    (select id from public.people where legacy_resource_id = 'RES-0105'),
    (select id from public.people where legacy_resource_id = 'RES-0102'),
    (select id from public.people where legacy_resource_id = 'RES-0109'),
    $ppm${"shortName":"Identity Platform","formerName":"","projectClassification":"Change","confidentialityClassification":"Confidential","portfolioId":"PORT-00001","portfolio":"Portfolio Manager","lifecycleTemplateId":"LIFE-00001","lifecycleTemplateVersion":1,"reportingCalendarId":"CAL-00001","approvalStatus":"Approved","sponsorConfirmationStatus":"Confirmed","requirementsApprovalStatus":"Approved","baselineApprovalStatus":"Approved","goLiveApprovalStatus":"Approved","closureApprovalStatus":"Not started","operationalReadinessStatus":"Complete","trainingStatus":"Complete","communicationsStatus":"Complete","testDatesStatus":"Complete","reportingFrequency":"Monthly","archived":false,"archivedAt":"","archiveReason":"","preArchiveStatus":"","stageOverrideReason":"","reasonForSlippage":"","returnToGreen":"","actualStartDate":"2025-07-07","actualEndDate":"","closureDate":"","approvedImplementationDate":"2026-07-31","indicativeCosts":800000,"costEstimate":780000,"benefitRag":"Green","qualityRag":"Green","operationalReadinessRag":"Green","calculatedRags":{},"ragOverrideJustifications":{},"defectsBlockers":"","deploymentDependencies":"","goLiveCriteria":"Met at each population migration; all criteria were satisfied.","supportModel":"Application support with the identity vendor as third line from 25 September.","hypercarePlan":"Eight weeks of daily monitoring reducing to weekly, completing 25 September. Nine tickets raised, all closed.","rollbackPlan":"Each population could revert to its legacy mechanism; not required for any population.","outstandingRisksIssues":"","closureSummary":"Delivered on the baseline date and within the approved budget. All three legacy authentication mechanisms are decommissioned and the 2024 audit finding is closed.","finalFinancialPosition":"Approved budget £780,000, final outturn £762,400, an underspend of £17,600 driven by lower than forecast vendor professional services.","outstandingActions":"Two actions remain: decommission the final legacy directory server, and complete the annual access review with the new platform's reporting. Both are transferring to Technology.","benefitsHandover":"Benefit measurement transfers to the Head of Technology Delivery, reporting quarterly for twelve months.","lessonsLearned":"Migrating colleagues first was the right call and built confidence. The member telephone fallback should have been designed earlier; it was added late under time pressure and would have been cheaper up front. Vendor professional services were over-estimated by about 20%.","archiveLocation":"","solutionOptions":"Extend the existing directory, adopt a cloud identity platform, or build a bespoke service. A cloud identity platform was chosen on security capability and total cost.","operationalReadinessRequirements":"Service desk trained on the new reset process, member help content published, telephone route for members unable to use an authenticator app, and rollback per population.","testApproach":"Integration testing per application, a full penetration test after member migration, and an accessibility review of the member multi-factor journey.","implementationApproach":"Population by population, with each legacy mechanism kept live until the population was fully migrated.","discoveryDeliverables":"Current-state authentication assessment, vendor evaluation, migration approach, and a cost case.","deliveryPlanSummary":"Colleagues migrated first in the first quarter of 2026, advisers in the second, members in the third, with legacy decommissioning following each.","detailedResourceDemand":"Two identity engineers, one security architect at 50%, one tester, and a change lead for member communications. Now one engineer in hypercare.","resourceDemandSummary":"Peak demand 5.5 FTE, now 1.2 FTE in hypercare.","initialResourceRequirements":"Estimated 5 to 6 FTE with identity specialism.","initialRaidSummary":"Member adoption of multi-factor authentication, application integration effort, and lockout risk during migration were raised at intake. All were managed and closed.","assumptionsConstraints":"Assumed member adoption of multi-factor would need a supported route for members without smartphones, which was built. Constrained by a requirement that no member is locked out during migration.","strategicDependencies":"PRJ-00006 and PRJ-00009 both depend on this platform for their multi-factor authentication, and both are now unblocked.","deliveryDependencies":"None outstanding. All application integrations are complete.","successMeasures":"Multi-factor coverage, password reset call volume, legacy platforms decommissioned, and audit finding status.","benefitMeasures":"Service desk reporting, identity platform coverage reports, and the audit tracker.","expectedBenefits":"Audit finding closed, multi-factor authentication on 100% of accounts, about 100 service desk calls a month avoided worth roughly £42,000 a year, and three legacy platforms decommissioned.","customerOutcome":"Members get a modern sign-in with multi-factor protection and can reset their own password.","regulatoryDriver":"FCA operational resilience expectations and the 2024 internal audit finding on authentication controls.","mandatoryDeliveryDate":"","nextStageGateDate":"2026-09-25","currentStageGate":"Gate 6 - In hypercare","requestor":"Stephen Nkemelu","requestorResourceId":"RES-0109","requestorEmail":"stephen.nkemelu@example.com","projectManager":"Aisha Farouk","projectManagerResourceId":"RES-0105","projectManagerEmail":"aisha.farouk@example.com","sponsor":"Daniel Whitfield","sponsorResourceId":"RES-0102","sponsorEmail":"daniel.whitfield@example.com","projectLead":"Stephen Nkemelu","projectLeadResourceId":"RES-0109","projectLeadEmail":"stephen.nkemelu@example.com","deputyProjectManager":"","deputyProjectManagerResourceId":"","deputyProjectManagerEmail":"","businessOwner":"Stephen Nkemelu","businessOwnerResourceId":"RES-0109","businessOwnerEmail":"stephen.nkemelu@example.com","technicalLead":"Stephen Nkemelu","technicalLeadResourceId":"RES-0109","technicalLeadEmail":"stephen.nkemelu@example.com","businessAnalyst":"Joseph Adeyemi","businessAnalystResourceId":"RES-0113","businessAnalystEmail":"joseph.adeyemi@example.com","testLead":"Ffion Davies","testLeadResourceId":"RES-0114","testLeadEmail":"ffion.davies@example.com","changeLead":"Dominic Fry","changeLeadResourceId":"RES-0120","changeLeadEmail":"dominic.fry@example.com","financeContact":"Martin Cole","financeContactResourceId":"RES-0115","financeContactEmail":"martin.cole@example.com","complianceContact":"Yvonne Baptiste","complianceContactResourceId":"RES-0116","complianceContactEmail":"yvonne.baptiste@example.com","benefitOwner":"Stephen Nkemelu","benefitOwnerResourceId":"RES-0109","benefitOwnerEmail":"stephen.nkemelu@example.com","projectCode":"PRJ-00016","projectName":"Identity and Access Platform","description":"Replacement of three separate authentication mechanisms with a single identity platform covering colleagues, members and advisers, including multi-factor authentication throughout.","programmeId":"PRG-00005","programme":"BAU","workstream":"BAU","businessArea":"Technology","projectType":"Technology","priority":"Critical","projectStatus":"Active","currentStage":"Hypercare","nextStage":"Closure","overallRag":"Green","scheduleRag":"Green","scopeRag":"Green","financialRag":"Green","resourceRag":"Green","riskRag":"Green","deliveryConfidence":"High","baselineStartDate":"2025-07-07","baselineEndDate":"2026-09-25","forecastStartDate":"2025-07-07","forecastEndDate":"2026-09-25","targetImplementationDate":"2026-07-31","percentageComplete":96,"dateLogged":"2025-04-14","proposedStartDate":"2025-07-07","currentPosition":"All three populations are migrated and multi-factor authentication is enforced. Hypercare has been quiet: nine tickets in four weeks, all resolved, none critical. Closure documentation is being assembled.","nextSteps":"Complete the closure report and lessons learned, hand over to application support on 25 September, and close the project at the September governance meeting.","highLevelScope":"Single identity platform for colleague, member and adviser authentication; multi-factor authentication for all three; single sign-on across internal applications; self-service password reset; and decommissioning of the three legacy authentication mechanisms.","outOfScope":"Privileged access management and device management, both handled by separate security workstreams.","inScope":"All internal applications, the member area, and the adviser portal.","businessProblem":"Three separate authentication mechanisms, none with enforced multi-factor authentication, and password resets consuming about 120 service desk calls a month. Flagged as a high finding in the 2024 penetration test and by Internal Audit.","desiredOutcome":"One identity platform with multi-factor authentication enforced everywhere, self-service resets, and the audit finding closed.","businessPriority":"Critical","strategicDriver":"Close a known security gap and reduce service desk load","strategicObjective":"Secure and supportable technology estate","additionalStakeholders":"Information Security, Internal Audit, the service desk, and every application owner.","fundingSource":"Technology and security budget","demoDataSet":"STAGE-14A"}$ppm$::jsonb
on conflict (project_code) do nothing;

